2d:["$","$L3f",null,{"records":[{"slug":"rajasthan-oxytocin-2026","title":"Rajasthan Oxytocin Quality Investigation","origin":"historical-case","categories":["drug-quality","substandard-or-falsified","adverse-event","regulatory-action"],"statuses":["reported-by-media","historical-case","causality-not-established"],"products":[{"name":"TOCIN","form":"Oxytocin injection (5 ml and 1 ml reported)","activeIngredients":["Oxytocin"],"batches":[],"batchNote":"No batch or lot numbers are published in the sources read. Reports describe a 5 ml batch and a different 1 ml batch."}],"location":{"city":"Kota","state":"Rajasthan","country":"India"},"eventDate":{"label":"May 2026 (reported)","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]},"summary":"After five women died following childbirth at two Kota hospitals, Rajasthan banned a TOCIN oxytocin injection whose sample failed quality testing, and later cancelled a Kota distributor’s licence. State and AIIMS investigations reported by The Indian Express did not attribute the deaths to the ineffective drug, and described gaps in clinical monitoring and documentation.","whyItMatters":"A product failed testing and regulators acted on its supply chain, yet the reports describe more than one batch and no proven link to the deaths. Separating what is verified from what is assumed is the whole investigation.","parties":[{"role":"manufacturer","name":"Jackson Laboratories Pvt Ltd","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"],"note":"Named as the manufacturer of TOCIN in public reporting. A separate report calls the maker of Tocin 1 ml “an Amritsar-based company” without naming it."},{"role":"distributor","name":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall","place":"Indraprastha Industrial Area, Kota","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"],"note":"Wholesale drug licences and Schedule X licence reported cancelled."},{"role":"laboratory","name":"Rajasthan Drug Testing Laboratory","place":"Jaipur","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"],"note":"Reported to have found no trace of oxytocin in a 1 ml batch."},{"role":"regulator","name":"Drug Control Department, Rajasthan","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-06-26"]},{"role":"hospital","name":"JK Lone Hospital","place":"Kota","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"],"note":"Two of the five deaths reported here."},{"role":"hospital","name":"New Medical College Hospital","place":"Kota","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"],"note":"Three of the five deaths reported here."},{"role":"investigator","name":"Eight-member expert committee, Government of Rajasthan","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"role":"investigator","name":"Six-member expert team, AIIMS","place":"New Delhi","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}],"statements":[{"text":"Five women died after childbirth by caesarean section at hospitals in Kota.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"TOCIN oxytocin injection failed laboratory testing for its oxytocin content.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-06-26"]},{"text":"Rajasthan’s Drug Control Department took regulatory action against the TOCIN supply chain.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-06-26"]},{"text":"Rajasthan’s Drug Control Department banned the sale and use of TOCIN (Oxytocin Injection 5 ml) after a sample failed quality tests.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"The Drug Controller said the 5 ml sample passed bacterial endotoxin and sterility tests but did not contain the required quantity of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"],"quote":"the required quantity of oxytocin was not found in the injection"},{"text":"Around 3,500 vials were seized from Kota government hospital and other stockists linked to the supply chain.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"Officials said the banned 5 ml injection belonged to a different batch from the 1 ml injections of the same company that the Kota medical college procured locally.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"The Rajasthan Drug Testing Laboratory in Jaipur declared a batch of Tocin 1 ml spurious after tests found no trace of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"],"quote":"contained no trace of oxytocin, its active ingredient"},{"text":"A Kota distributor was alleged to have bought 9,300 units of Tocin 1 ml but sold 10,050 from the same batch; its wholesale and Schedule X licences were cancelled.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"text":"Regulators from three states, along with the apex drug controller, were reported to have acted against the manufacturer and distributor. The states are not named.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"The Rajasthan expert committee did not attribute the deaths to the missing oxytocin.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"],"quote":"the absence of active pharmaceutical ingredient oxytocin cannot be attributed to mortality"},{"text":"Investigators found the five women died of different medical conditions, with no single common cause.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Investigators reported missing records of hourly blood pressure and pulse, urine output, liver function tests and medication administration, and no autopsy in two cases.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Earlier, the Drug Controller said the banned injections had no direct link with the deaths, as the women had caesarean deliveries.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"gaps":["No batch or lot numbers appear in any source read.","Whether the 1 ml injections used at the Kota hospitals came from the batch declared spurious is not stated.","The three states whose regulators acted are not named.","The ban order, licence-cancellation order and laboratory reports have not been read directly — only as reported.","The committee reports are unreleased; their findings are known only as reported by The Indian Express.","Distribution beyond Kota stockists is not documented in the sources read."],"sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"],"history":[{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"source-read","change":"Read by hand: The Times of India, 25 May 2026."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"source-read","change":"Read by hand: The Indian Express, 26 Jun 2026."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"source-read","change":"Read by hand: The Indian Express, 6 Jul 2026."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"created","change":"Record created from three media sources."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"classified","change":"Each statement labelled by how well its sources support it."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"correction","change":"A laboratory finding re-labelled from corroborated to single report: both supporting articles are from the same outlet."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"correction","change":"An inferred manufacturer location (Amritsar) removed: the report that mentions it does not name the company."}],"timeline":[{"date":null,"dateLabel":"May 2026, before 25 May · exact dates not stated","kind":"clinical","title":"Five women die after childbirth at two Kota hospitals","detail":"The deaths followed caesarean deliveries at JK Lone Hospital and New Medical College Hospital.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]},{"date":"2026-05-19","dateLabel":"19 May 2026","kind":"regulatory","title":"Drug officials inspect a Kota distributor","detail":"Officials inspected M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall and reported a missing inspection register and no qualified pharmacist on site.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Test date not stated · reported 25 May 2026","kind":"testing","title":"A TOCIN 5 ml sample is reported to fail testing","detail":"The Drug Controller said the required quantity of oxytocin was not found; the sample passed bacterial endotoxin and sterility tests.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"date":"2026-05-25","dateLabel":"25 May 2026","kind":"regulatory","title":"Rajasthan bans the sale and use of TOCIN 5 ml","detail":"Orders were issued across the state, and around 3,500 vials were seized from Kota government hospital and other stockists.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 26 Jun 2026","kind":"testing","title":"A Tocin 1 ml batch is declared spurious","detail":"The Rajasthan Drug Testing Laboratory, Jaipur, reported no trace of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 26 Jun 2026","kind":"regulatory","title":"The Kota distributor’s licences are cancelled","detail":"Its wholesale drug licences and Schedule X licence were cancelled with immediate effect over alleged irregularities, including selling more Tocin 1 ml than it bought.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 6 Jul 2026","kind":"regulatory","title":"Regulators in three states and the apex drug controller act","detail":"Action was reported against the manufacturer and the distributor. The states are not named.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 6 Jul 2026","kind":"investigation","title":"WHO seeks information on a possible link","detail":"WHO was reported to have sought information on a possible link to ineffective oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 6 Jul 2026","kind":"investigation","title":"State committee and AIIMS team do not attribute the deaths to the drug","detail":"An eight-member committee reviewed the records of 12 patients who died or had severe complications. It reported different causes of death and gaps in monitoring and documentation. The reports are unreleased.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Status not stated","kind":"regulatory","title":"Judicial proceedings","detail":"The licence cancellation was described as independent of any judicial proceedings “currently pending or may be initiated”. Their status is not stated.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}],"workspace":{"batchLanes":[{"label":"TOCIN 5 ml","batchNumber":null,"facts":[{"text":"A sample failed quality testing: the required quantity of oxytocin was not found.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"Sale and use were banned across Rajasthan on 25 May 2026.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"Officials said this batch was different from the 1 ml injections the Kota medical college procured.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"unknowns":["Batch number","Where else this batch was distributed","Whether any of it was given at the Kota hospitals"]},{"label":"Tocin 1 ml","batchNumber":null,"facts":[{"text":"Procured locally by the Kota medical college, from a different batch than the banned 5 ml.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"A 1 ml batch was declared spurious after tests found no trace of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"A Kota distributor allegedly bought 9,300 units and sold 10,050 from the same batch.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}],"unknowns":["Batch number","Whether the hospital’s 1 ml stock came from the spurious batch","Who bought the 10,050 units"]}],"batchConflict":"The two test results are described differently: “required quantity … not found” for 5 ml and “no trace” for 1 ml. They may describe different batches, so they are kept apart rather than merged.","distribution":[{"from":"Manufacturer (“an Amritsar-based company”)","to":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall, Kota","item":"Tocin 1 ml","quantity":"9,300 units purchased","status":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"from":"Manufacturer","to":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall, Kota","item":"Tocin 1 ml","quantity":"750 units","status":"not-established","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"],"note":"Claimed in a manufacturer’s letter to have been sent separately by bus. The Drug Control Department found the explanation unsatisfactory."},{"from":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall, Kota","to":"Buyers not named","item":"Tocin 1 ml, same batch","quantity":"10,050 units sold","status":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"from":"Supplier not named","to":"Kota medical college","item":"TOCIN 1 ml","quantity":"Not stated","status":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"],"note":"Procured locally. Officials said it was a different batch from the banned 5 ml."},{"from":"Kota government hospital and other stockists","to":"Seized by the Drug Control Department","item":"TOCIN vials (strength not stated)","quantity":"Around 3,500 vials","status":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"from":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall, Kota","to":"The two Kota hospitals","item":"Tocin 1 ml","status":"not-established","sourceIds":[],"note":"No source read links this distributor to the hospitals where the deaths occurred."}],"quantityCheck":{"label":"Distributor stock reconciliation · Tocin 1 ml, one batch","inLabel":"Purchased","inQty":9300,"outLabel":"Sold","outQty":10050,"explanation":"The firm said the difference was sent separately by bus. The Drug Control Department found that explanation unsatisfactory.","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},"clinical":{"availability":"No administration records, dosing times or patient-level timelines are public. Only the aggregate findings below were reported, from unreleased investigation reports.","items":[{"text":"Two deaths were recorded at JK Lone Hospital: one attributed to pre-existing heart disease, one to complications of postpartum haemorrhage.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Three deaths were recorded at New Medical College Hospital, attributed to disseminated intravascular coagulation, hypovolemic shock and stitch chorioamnionitis.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"The committee noted that clinical records did not mention additional oxytocic or uterotonic medicines in any case.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"],"quote":"in no case there has been any mention of having been given additional oxytocic or uterotonic medications as per clinical records"},{"text":"Autopsies were not conducted in two cases where they could have established the cause of death.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},"reviewSteps":["Obtain the ban order and the laboratory report for the 5 ml sample, including its batch number.","Obtain the laboratory report that declared the 1 ml batch spurious, including its batch number.","Compare both batch numbers with the Kota hospitals’ pharmacy issue records.","Request the distributor’s purchase and sale invoices and the manufacturer’s dispatch letter, and reconcile the 750-unit difference.","Through authorised access only, review medication administration records for the 12 patients the committee examined.","Confirm with regulators which three states acted, and on which products and batches.","Record each conclusion with its evidence, the reviewer and the reason."],"support":[{"area":"Product identity","how":"Match brand, strength, form and manufacturer across every record before linking them.","here":"Two strengths, 5 ml and 1 ml, are reported. They stay separate."},{"area":"Batch","how":"Tie each test result and each stock record to a batch number, and refuse links made on brand name alone.","here":"Neither batch number is public."},{"area":"Distribution","how":"Reconcile purchase, sale and dispatch documents and flag any quantity difference.","here":"Reported purchases and sales differ by 750 units."},{"area":"Storage","how":"Attach cold-chain and storage records to each batch.","here":"Oxytocin needs storage at 2–8 °C; improper storage of finished products was reported."},{"area":"Administration","how":"Link pharmacy issue and administration records to the batch given to each patient.","here":"Reviewed clinical records did not mention additional oxytocic medicines."},{"area":"Clinical","how":"Lay monitoring records on one timeline and mark every missing entry.","here":"Hourly blood pressure, pulse and other monitoring records were reported missing."},{"area":"Regulatory","how":"Keep orders and laboratory reports as source documents, with their dates.","here":"The orders and reports are known here only through media coverage."}],"map":{"places":[{"id":"kota","name":"Kota","region":"Rajasthan","lat":25.21,"lon":75.86,"state":"reported-distribution","role":"Deaths, a distributor and seizures","when":"May–June 2026","batchEvidence":"Tocin 1 ml and TOCIN 5 ml both reported here. No batch number is published.","evidence":[{"text":"A Kota distributor allegedly sold 10,050 units of Tocin 1 ml from a batch later declared spurious.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"text":"Around 3,500 vials were seized from Kota government hospital and other stockists.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"The Kota medical college procured 1 ml injections locally, from a batch other than the banned 5 ml.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"Five women died after childbirth at JK Lone Hospital and New Medical College Hospital. Investigators did not attribute the deaths to the drug.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"id":"jaipur","name":"Jaipur","region":"Rajasthan","lat":26.91,"lon":75.79,"state":"investigation-site","role":"Rajasthan Drug Testing Laboratory","when":"Date not stated","batchEvidence":"Tested a Tocin 1 ml batch. Not reported as a place the product was distributed.","evidence":[{"text":"The laboratory declared a Tocin 1 ml batch spurious after tests found no trace of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"id":"new-delhi","name":"New Delhi","region":"Delhi","lat":28.61,"lon":77.21,"state":"investigation-site","role":"AIIMS expert team","when":"Date not stated","batchEvidence":"No source reports the product reaching New Delhi.","evidence":[{"text":"A six-member team from AIIMS, New Delhi, reported to the Rajasthan committee, including on infection control.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"id":"bikaner","name":"Bikaner","region":"Rajasthan","lat":28.02,"lon":73.31,"state":"not-established","role":"Later maternal deaths","when":"After the Kota deaths","batchEvidence":"No source mentions TOCIN or any batch here.","evidence":[{"text":"Maternal deaths in Bikaner followed those in Kota. The state government delinked them from Kota and attributed them to complications of high-risk pregnancies.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"id":"jodhpur","name":"Jodhpur","region":"Rajasthan","lat":26.24,"lon":73.02,"state":"not-established","role":"Later maternal deaths","when":"After the Kota deaths","batchEvidence":"No source mentions TOCIN or any batch here.","evidence":[{"text":"Maternal deaths in Jodhpur followed those in Kota. The state government delinked them from Kota and attributed them to complications of high-risk pregnancies.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"id":"amritsar","name":"Amritsar","region":"Punjab","lat":31.63,"lon":74.87,"state":"supply-origin","role":"Reported base of the Tocin 1 ml maker","when":"Not applicable","batchEvidence":"The source does not name the company or give a batch number.","evidence":[{"text":"The Tocin 1 ml bought by the Kota distributor was described as made by “an Amritsar-based company”.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}]}],"unplaced":[{"text":"Regulators from three states, along with the apex drug controller, were reported to have acted. The states are not named, so they cannot be placed.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Buyers of the 10,050 units sold by the Kota distributor are not named, so where that stock went is unknown.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}]},"graph":{"nodes":[{"id":"mfr","stage":"manufacturer","lane":0.5,"label":"Jackson Laboratories Pvt Ltd","sub":"Named as TOCIN maker in reporting","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Named as the manufacturer of TOCIN (Oxytocin Injection 5 ml).","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"text":"Named as the manufacturer of the spurious oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}],"missing":["Manufacturing and release records for both batches","Raw testing data"],"conflicts":["One report names the Tocin 1 ml maker only as “an Amritsar-based company”, without naming it.","Investigators reported the company could not produce raw testing data."]},{"id":"b1","stage":"batch","lane":0,"label":"Tocin 1 ml","sub":"Batch declared spurious · no. not published","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Declared spurious by the Rajasthan Drug Testing Laboratory: no trace of oxytocin.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26","ie-2026-07-06"]}],"missing":["Batch number","Laboratory report"],"conflicts":["Described as “no trace” of oxytocin, while the 5 ml sample was “required quantity … not found”."]},{"id":"b5","stage":"batch","lane":1,"label":"TOCIN 5 ml","sub":"Sample failed · no. not published","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"A sample did not contain the required quantity of oxytocin; sale and use banned on 25 May 2026.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"missing":["Batch number","Ban order","Laboratory report"]},{"id":"dist","stage":"distributor","lane":0,"label":"M/s Rajasthan Medical Hall","sub":"Kota · licences cancelled","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Alleged to have bought 9,300 and sold 10,050 units of Tocin 1 ml from the same batch.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"text":"Wholesale drug licences and Schedule X licence cancelled.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}],"quantities":[{"label":"Purchased","value":"9,300","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"label":"Sold","value":"10,050","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"label":"Claimed sent by bus","value":"750","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]}],"missing":["Purchase invoices","Sale invoices","The manufacturer’s dispatch letter (described, not public)"],"conflicts":["Sold 750 more units than it bought; the explanation was found unsatisfactory."]},{"id":"dist5","stage":"distributor","lane":1,"label":"Distributor not named","sub":"For TOCIN 5 ml","known":false,"facts":[],"missing":["Name of the distributor","Dispatch and sale records"]},{"id":"buyers","stage":"wholesaler","lane":0,"label":"Buyers not named","sub":"10,050 units sold","known":false,"facts":[],"missing":["List of buyers","Sale invoices"]},{"id":"stockists","stage":"wholesaler","lane":1,"label":"Kota stockists","sub":"Vials seized · strength not stated","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Around 3,500 vials were seized from Kota government hospital and other stockists linked to the supply chain.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"missing":["Seizure inventory with strengths and batch numbers"]},{"id":"kmc","stage":"hospital","lane":0,"label":"Kota medical college","sub":"1 ml procured locally","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Procured 1 ml injections of the same company locally, from a batch other than the banned 5 ml.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"missing":["Procurement record and supplier name","Batch number of stock held"],"conflicts":["Whether this is one of the two hospitals where the deaths occurred is not stated."]},{"id":"kgh","stage":"hospital","lane":1,"label":"Kota government hospital","sub":"Vials seized","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Named as one of the places vials were seized from.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]}],"missing":["Which hospital, and the strength and batch of the seized vials"]},{"id":"admin","stage":"administration","lane":0.5,"label":"Administration records","sub":"Not public","known":false,"facts":[{"text":"The committee noted clinical records did not mention additional oxytocic or uterotonic medicines in any case.","basis":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}],"missing":["Pharmacy issue records","Medication administration records with batch numbers"]},{"id":"deaths","stage":"report","lane":0.5,"label":"Five maternal deaths","sub":"Reported · causality not established","known":true,"facts":[{"text":"Five women died after childbirth by caesarean section at two Kota hospitals.","basis":"corroborated","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"The state committee said the absence of oxytocin cannot be attributed to mortality.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}],"missing":["Formal safety reports or adverse-event reports for these cases"]}],"edges":[{"from":"mfr","to":"b1","status":"reported","note":"Reporting names the company as maker of the spurious oxytocin; another report names only “an Amritsar-based company”.","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06","ie-2026-06-26"]},{"from":"mfr","to":"b5","status":"reported","note":"The ban names TOCIN 5 ml as manufactured by the company.","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"from":"b1","to":"dist","status":"reported","note":"The distributor allegedly bought and sold units from the batch declared spurious.","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"from":"b5","to":"dist5","status":"unverified","note":"No source names who distributed the 5 ml batch.","sourceIds":[]},{"from":"dist","to":"buyers","status":"reported","note":"10,050 units allegedly sold. The buyers are not named.","sourceIds":["ie-2026-06-26"]},{"from":"dist5","to":"stockists","status":"unverified","note":"Vials were seized from stockists “linked to the medicine’s supply chain”. Their strength and batch are not stated.","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"from":"buyers","to":"kmc","status":"unverified","note":"No source says the medical college’s 1 ml stock came from this distributor or from the spurious batch.","sourceIds":[]},{"from":"stockists","to":"kgh","status":"reported","note":"Vials were seized from Kota government hospital as well as stockists.","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25"]},{"from":"kmc","to":"admin","status":"unverified","note":"No administration record is public.","sourceIds":[]},{"from":"kgh","to":"admin","status":"unverified","note":"No administration record is public.","sourceIds":[]},{"from":"admin","to":"deaths","status":"inferred","note":"Public reporting connected the deaths with the drug. The state committee did not attribute the deaths to it.","sourceIds":["toi-2026-05-25","ie-2026-07-06"]}]},"comparison":{"columns":[{"label":"JK Lone Hospital","sub":"Kota"},{"label":"New Medical College Hospital","sub":"Kota"},{"label":"Bikaner and Jodhpur","sub":"Later deaths"}],"rows":[{"label":"Drug and batch identity","cells":[{"text":"Not stated for this hospital.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"Not stated for this hospital.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"No product mentioned.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]}]},{"label":"Manufacturer and distributor","cells":[{"text":"Not stated for this hospital.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"Not stated for this hospital.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"Not mentioned.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]}]},{"label":"Administration dates","cells":[{"text":"Not public.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"Not public.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"Not public.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]}]},{"label":"Clinical chronology","cells":[{"text":"Not public. Monitoring records were reported missing.","state":"missing","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Not public. Monitoring records were reported missing.","state":"missing","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Not reported.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]}]},{"label":"Reported outcomes","cells":[{"text":"Two deaths: one from pre-existing heart disease, one from complications of postpartum haemorrhage.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Three deaths: disseminated intravascular coagulation, hypovolemic shock, stitch chorioamnionitis.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Maternal deaths reported; number not stated.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"label":"Product-quality test results","cells":[{"text":"No result linked to this hospital’s stock.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"No result linked to this hospital’s stock.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]},{"text":"None.","state":"missing","sourceIds":[]}]},{"label":"Other medicines and context","cells":[{"text":"Records did not mention additional oxytocic medicines. 25 maternal deaths in 2025; 4 in 2026 at the time of reporting.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Records did not mention additional oxytocic medicines. 14 maternal deaths in 2025; 3 in 2026 at the time of reporting.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Attributed by the state to complications of high-risk pregnancies.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]},{"label":"Investigation findings","cells":[{"text":"Deaths not attributed to the drug; gaps in monitoring and documentation.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Deaths not attributed to the drug; gaps in monitoring and documentation.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]},{"text":"Delinked from Kota by the state government.","state":"reported","sourceIds":["ie-2026-07-06"]}]}],"similar":["Both Kota hospitals: deaths after caesarean delivery, within about a week.","Both Kota hospitals: the same documentation and monitoring gaps were reported."],"different":["Every death was attributed to a different medical condition.","Bikaner and Jodhpur were delinked from Kota by the state government."],"missing":["Which product and batch, if any, each patient received.","Administration dates and clinical timelines for every hospital."]}}},{"slug":"india-contaminated-oral-liquids-2025","title":"Contaminated Oral Liquid Medicines, India","origin":"historical-case","categories":["drug-quality","substandard-or-falsified","regulatory-action","official-alert"],"statuses":["official-alert","historical-case"],"products":[{"name":"COLDRIF","form":"Oral liquid","activeIngredients":["Paracetamol","Chlorpheniramine maleate","Phenylephrine","Sodium citrate"],"batches":[{"batch":"SR-13","manufactured":"05/2025","expires":"04/2027","finding":"48.6% w/v DEG (as reported by CDSCO)","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}]},{"name":"Respifresh TR","form":"Oral liquid","activeIngredients":["Bromhexine hydrochloride","Terbutaline sulphate","Guaiphenesin","Menthol"],"batches":[{"batch":"R01GL2523","manufactured":"01/2025","expires":"12/2026","finding":"1.34% w/v DEG (as reported by CDSCO)","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}]},{"name":"ReLife","form":"Oral liquid","activeIngredients":["Ambroxol HCl","Guaiphenesin","Terbutaline sulphate","Menthol"],"batches":[{"batch":"LSL25160","manufactured":"01/2025","expires":"12/2026","finding":"0.61% w/v DEG (as reported by CDSCO)","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}]}],"location":{"country":"India","note":"The alert does not state where the illnesses occurred."},"eventDate":{"label":"Identified by WHO on 30 Sep 2025","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},"summary":"WHO Medical Product Alert N°5/2025 names specific batches of three oral liquid medicines found to contain diethylene glycol (DEG), reported to WHO by India’s CDSCO on 8 October 2025 after clusters of acute illness and child deaths.","whyItMatters":"The alert names exact batches, not whole brands. Any investigation has to match product, batch and manufacturer before treating a report as related.","parties":[{"role":"manufacturer","name":"Sresan Pharmaceutical","place":"Kancheepuram","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"],"note":"COLDRIF, batch SR-13."},{"role":"manufacturer","name":"Rednex Pharmaceutical Pvt Ltd.","place":"Bavla, Ahmedabad, Gujarat","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"],"note":"Respifresh TR, batch R01GL2523."},{"role":"manufacturer","name":"Shape Pharma Pvt. Ltd.","place":"Shekhpur, Gujarat","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"],"note":"ReLife, batch LSL25160."},{"role":"regulator","name":"Central Drugs Standard Control Organization (CDSCO)","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"],"note":"Reported DEG in at least three oral liquid medicines to WHO on 8 October 2025."}],"statements":[{"text":"On 30 September 2025, WHO identified information on localised clusters of acute illness and child fatalities in India.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"On 8 October 2025, CDSCO reported to WHO the presence of diethylene glycol in at least three oral liquid medicines.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"CDSCO informed WHO that the contaminated products were reportedly consumed by the affected children.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"],"quote":"reportedly consumed by the affected children"},{"text":"The contaminated medicines are specific batches of COLDRIF, Respifresh TR and ReLife.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"State authorities ordered an immediate halt to production at the implicated sites, suspended product authorisations and initiated a recall.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"CDSCO informed WHO that none of the contaminated medicines had been exported and there was no evidence of illegal export.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"WHO advised regulators to evaluate oral liquid medicines from the same manufacturing sites, particularly those produced since December 2024.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}],"scopeNote":"Only the three batches below are named in the alert. It does not say that other batches, or every product sold under these brand names, are affected.","healthConcerns":[{"text":"Diethylene glycol is toxic to humans when consumed and can prove fatal. Use, especially in children, may result in serious injury or death.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"Toxic effects listed by WHO include abdominal pain, vomiting, diarrhoea, inability to pass urine, headache, altered mental state and acute kidney injury, which may lead to death.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"The alert describes clusters of acute illness and child fatalities, but gives no number of cases or deaths.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}],"actions":[{"text":"State authorities ordered an immediate halt to production at the implicated manufacturing sites.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"State authorities suspended product authorisations and initiated a recall of the contaminated products.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"WHO advised regulators to consider targeted market surveillance, especially of informal and unregulated supply chains.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"text":"WHO asked authorities to notify it immediately if these products are detected in their country.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}],"timeline":[{"date":"2024-12-01","dateLabel":"December 2024 onwards","kind":"regulatory","title":"Production window WHO asks regulators to review","detail":"WHO advised evaluating oral liquid medicines from the same sites, particularly those produced since December 2024.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"date":"2025-09-30","dateLabel":"30 Sep 2025","kind":"clinical","title":"WHO identifies clusters of acute illness and child deaths in India","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"date":"2025-10-08","dateLabel":"8 Oct 2025","kind":"testing","title":"CDSCO reports diethylene glycol in at least three oral liquid medicines to WHO","detail":"Contamination levels in the annex are as reported by CDSCO: 48.6%, 1.34% and 0.61% w/v DEG.","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Date not stated · reported 13 Oct 2025","kind":"regulatory","title":"State authorities halt production, suspend authorisations and start a recall","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"date":"2025-10-13","dateLabel":"13 Oct 2025","kind":"regulatory","title":"WHO publishes Medical Product Alert N°5/2025","basis":"official","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"]},{"date":null,"dateLabel":"Open at publication","kind":"investigation","title":"Source of the contamination","detail":"WHO said it continues to work with Indian authorities to identify the source of the contamination.","basis":"not-established","sourceIds":["who-n5-2025-pdf"]}],"gaps":["The alert does not state where the illnesses occurred or how many children were affected.","The source of the contamination was still being identified when the alert was published.","Only the listed batches are named; the alert does not say whether other batches were tested."],"sourceIds":["who-n5-2025","who-n5-2025-pdf"],"history":[{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"source-read","change":"Read by hand: WHO alert page, 13 Oct 2025."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"source-read","change":"Read by hand: WHO alert PDF with annex, 13 Oct 2025."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"created","change":"Record created from the WHO alert."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"classified","change":"Each statement labelled by how well its sources support it."},{"on":"2026-10-27","kind":"correction","change":"A state name (Tamil Nadu) removed from a manufacturer address: the alert does not state it."}]}]}]
